 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Mi, tu, su",
   "texto": [
    "French possesives change as they are possessed by masculine, feminine or plural.",
    "**mon père** (my father), **ma mère** (my mother), **mes parents** (my parents).",
    "Same with «tu»: **ton, ta, tes**. And with «su» (of him or of her): **son, sa, ses**.",
    "Attention: **son frère** can be «his brother.» or «her brother.». What he commands is the gender of the possessed, not the one of the owner.",
    "In front of a feminine singular name that starts with vowel or **h** muda, **mon, ton, son**: **mon amie** (my friend) is used."
   ]
  },
  {
